re secure."},{"k":"p","t":"\u00b0 Never fail to connect the ground terminal."},{"k":"p","t":"\u00b0 Insert the power plug into a proper outlet and turn the power switch on."}]},{"n":6,"words":151,"blocks":[{"k":"li","t":"3. Handling Note and Warning"},{"k":"note","t":"Note:"},{"k":"p","t":"\u00b0 Erroneous or partial picture may appear on the screen when the machine is first switched on. This is typical of the characteristics of the CPU, and will correct itself"},{"k":"p","t":"automatically when the power switch is turned off and on."},{"k":"note","t":"Warning:"},{"k":"p","t":"\u00b0 Taito \"T.T. SPACE INVADERS\" uses a CPU and the latest solid-"},{"k":"p","t":"state circuitry for long life, however, as with sophisti-~ cated electronic equipment certain precautions must be observed to avoid damage."},{"k":"li","t":"(1) Do not attempt to service with ordinary testing equipment, since the internal voltage of the testing equipment may cause damage to the circuitry."},{"k":"li","t":"(2) Never connect or disconnect any of the solid~state modules while the power is on."},{"k":"p","t":"4, Routine Maintenance"},{"k":"p","t":"\u00b0 Owing to the solid-state electronic circuitry, this machine should require very little maintenance and only occasional adjustments, however, it is necessary to take measures to insure its daily safety."}]},{"n":7,"words":195,"blocks":[{"k":"p","t":"Playing Instructions"},{"k":"p","t":"One or two players."},{"k":"p","t":"Insert coin(s). 1 coin-1 play (3 Laser sases...Adjustable) 2 coins -2 plays (or 2 player game)"},{"k":"p","t":"Select one or two player game."},{"k":"p","t":"As the \"attacking sound\" is heard, invaders appear on the screen. Also, a laser base and four fortresses appear"},{"k":"p","t":"on the lower side of the screen."},{"k":"p","t":"To move the laser base left or right, push the control buttons."},{"k":"p","t":"To fire laser, push the fire button."},{"k":"p","t":"In two player mode, the play alternates between the two."},{"k":"p","t":"Scoring:"},{"k":"p","t":"eee eee seeveces. 20 pts."},{"k":"p","t":"ss ee ee eeeeeeeee 10 pts. oe"},{"k":"p","t":"Ge ee. 30 pts."},{"k":"p","t":"ey,"},{"k":"p","t":"="},{"k":"p","t":"Functional Description of Game:"},{"k":"p","t":"\u00b0 Invaders advance step by step against the laser base as they move left and right."},{"k":"p","t":"Fortresses are gradually destroyed by the attack of invaders. They are also destroyed by laser."},{"k":"p","t":"As the number of invaders decreases, they move fast."},{"k":"p","t":"UFO hit gives the player mystery score (50, 100, 150, or 300 points)."},{"k":"p","t":"When score reaches 1,500 points(adjustable), a bonus laser base appears with \u201cbeep\" sounds."},{"k":"p","t":"Game ends when all laser bases are hit by invader missiles or when invaders overrun the base."},{"k":"p","t":"Up to 99 coins can be credited."}]},{"n":8,"words":132,"blocks":[{"k":"li","t":"6. Adjustments on Power Supply P.C. Board"},{"k":"p","t":"(See Fig. 3)"},{"k":"note","t":"Caution: The line voltages should be set within the limits. Failure to do so may result in destruction of the"},{"k":"p","t":"Ic's."},{"k":"p","t":"\u00b0 To check the output voltages, measure them on the G-"},{"k":"p","t":"connector or the T-connector. (See the cable block diagram, AAROO166 in this manual.)"},{"k":"p","t":"@ +5V VR"},{"k":"p","t":"\u00ae)+12V vR (@) -sv va (\u00ae) -1av vA"},{"k":"p","t":"L_-_|"},{"k":"p","t":"Fig. 3"},{"k":"p","t":"\u00b0 +12V VR ... Pot for adjusting 12v line voltage (Adjustable range: 12V - 15V DC)"},{"k":"p","t":"\u00b0 -12V VR ... Pot for adjusting -12V line voltage (Adjustable range: -12v - -15V DC)"},{"k":"p","t":"\u00b0 + 5V VR... Pot for adjustable 5V line voltage (Adjustable range: 5V - 6V)"},{"k":"p","t":"\u00b0 - 5V VR... Pot for adjustable -5v line voltage (Adjustable range: -5V - -6V DC)"}]},{"n":9,"words":119,"blocks":[{"k":"li","t":"7. Adjustments on Game & Sound P.C. Board"},{"k":"p","t":"(See Fig. 4 and Tables 1 and 2)"},{"k":"p",